  "label": "The woman's exposed chest is mapped as the 'argumentative advantage' referenced in the text.",
  "description": "The top text 'hard to argue with a woman that's braless' implies that her physical appearance (specifically being braless) is the source of her persuasive power. The visual material shows her chest exposed through the wet, see-through shirt, which is directly mapped onto the textual claim that her 'bralessness' is the reason she is hard to argue with. This is an analogical mapping where the visual attribute (exposed chest) is equated with the textual concept (argumentative advantage).",
